        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add dev/release side-by-side app identity",
        "body": "## Motivation\n\nDev and release builds previously shared package/runtime state, so installing or testing one could disrupt the other. This makes the two variants genuinely side-by-side safe while preserving the contributor's compile-time identity design. Thanks @karkarl for the foundation.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Separate display/package/installer identities, install paths, data roots, mutexes, protocol handlers, autostart registry values, and scheduled tasks.\n- Exact protocol ownership: release accepts `openclaw://`; dev accepts `openclaw-dev://`.\n- Separate app-owned WSL gateways: `OpenClawGateway` on 18789 and `OpenClawGateway-Dev` on 18790.\n- Variant-aware onboarding, wizard log tailing, gateway registry/settings, updater behavior, in-app removal, and installer cleanup.\n- Target-only WSL cleanup: no global WSL shutdown; exact distro matching prevents release cleanup from touching dev keepalive processes.\n- Generated MSIX manifests under `obj`; dev packaging no longer mutates or leaks into the tracked release manifest.\n- Dev/release-aware local Inno build helper with published-identity validation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- AutoReview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Windows 11 ARM64 VM, exact head:\n  - full repository build: pass\n  - Shared tests: 2692 passed, 31 skipped\n  - SetupEngine tests: 376 passed\n  - Tray tests: 1535 passed\n  - native UI tests: 94 passed\n  - Dev build: 0 warnings, 0 errors\n- Dev and release processes launched simultaneously with distinct titles, data roots, registry protocol handlers, and deep-link routing.\n- Dev MSIX identity/protocol: `OpenClaw.Companion.Dev` / `openclaw-dev`; subsequent release package remained `OpenClaw.Companion` / `openclaw` and the source manifest remained unchanged.\n- Local Apple-silicon VM cannot provide nested virtualization for real WSL2; exact-head Windows CI setup E2E remains the authoritative WSL install/connect proof.\n",
        "branch": "karkarl-dev-release-side-by-side-identity",
